---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import SectionDivider from '../components/SectionDivider.astro';
import KashidaBorder from '../components/KashidaBorder.astro';
import ChinaLeaf from '../components/ChinaLeaf.astro';
import ShikaraIcon from '../components/ShikaraIcon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Biography - Abdul Aziz Bhat"
  description="The extraordinary life story of Abdul Aziz Bhat (1916-2016), from self-taught scholar in Bhalessa village to founding father of the University of Kashmir."
>
  <Hero
    variant="page"
    title="The Life of Abdul Aziz Bhat"
    subtitle="A Journey of Resilience, Education, and Transformation"
    quote="Education was not given to me—I claimed it for myself. And then I gave it to thousands."
  />

  <!-- Early Life Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center mb-8">
          <ChinaLeaf size="md" color="burgundy" class="mr-4" />
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-0">
            Early Life in Bhalessa (1916-1930s)
          </h2>
        </div>

        <KashidaBorder variant="vine" height="50px" class="mb-8 opacity-30" />

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-kashmir-lake-blue/90 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            <strong>Abdul Aziz Bhat</strong> was born in <strong>1916</strong> in the small village of
            <strong>Bhalessa, Kashmir</strong>—a place where education was rare, and the future seemed
            predetermined by one's birthplace.
          </p>

          <div class="kashmir-card p-6 my-8 bg-kashmir-cream/50">
            <p class="text-base italic mb-0">
              In Bhalessa, only <strong>14 people</strong> out of the entire village became educated during
              his generation. Among them were Abdul Aziz Bhat and <strong>Ghulam Rasool Azad</strong>.
              To be educated in Bhalessa was to be extraordinary.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p>
            What made Abdul Aziz even more remarkable was that he was <strong>self-taught</strong>. As a child,
            he taught himself to read—an act of will that would define his entire life. In a time and place
            where formal education was scarce, he created his own path through sheer determination.
          </p>

          <p>
            His family lived between two villages: <strong>Bhalessa and Bhaderwa</strong>, both in Kashmir.
            It was in these humble surroundings that young Abdul Aziz developed an insatiable appetite for
            knowledge and a vision that extended far beyond the mountains that surrounded him.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="leaf" />

  <!-- Education Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-gradient-to-b from-kashmir-cream to-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center mb-8">
          <ShikaraIcon size="md" variant="ornate" color="blue" class="mr-4" />
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-0">
            The Journey of Education
          </h2>
        </div>

        <KashidaBorder variant="floral" height="50px" class="mb-8 opacity-30" />

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <Card title="Early Education" variant="bordered" showLeafWatermark={true}>
            <p>
              Abdul Aziz began his formal education at the <strong>Bhalessa village school</strong>, though much
              of his early learning was self-directed. His natural ability to teach himself would serve him
              throughout his life.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card title="Higher Education in Kashmir & Jammu" variant="bordered" showLeafWatermark={true}>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-2 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <span><strong>Bhaderwa Degree College, Kashmir</strong> - Undergraduate studies</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-2 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <span><strong>GGM Science College, Jammu</strong> - Advanced studies and early teaching career</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </Card>

          <Card title="Professional Degrees" variant="bordered" showLeafWatermark={true}>
            <ul class="space-y-3">
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-2 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <span><strong>LLB (Bachelor of Laws)</strong> from <strong>Aligarh Muslim University</strong> - One of India's most prestigious institutions</span>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-2 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <span><strong>PhD in Education</strong> from <strong>University of Kashmir</strong> - The very institution he helped found</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </Card>

          <div class="kashmir-card p-8 dal-lake-bg text-white">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">Academic Specializations</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">
              Abdul Aziz Bhat became a distinguished scholar across multiple disciplines:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              <li>✦ <strong>English Literature & Language</strong></li>
              <li>✦ <strong>Social Work & Community Development</strong></li>
              <li>✦ <strong>Education & Pedagogy</strong></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="shikara" />

  <!-- Early Career Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-8 text-center">
          Early Career (Pre-1947)
        </h2>

        <KashidaBorder variant="geometric" height="50px" class="mb-8 opacity-30" />

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <Card title="Principal - Hari Singh High School" variant="bordered">
            <p>
              Before Partition, Abdul Aziz served as the <strong>Principal of Hari Singh High School</strong>,
              demonstrating leadership and educational vision at a young age. He was shaping young minds and
              building educational institutions even then.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card title="Lecturer - GGM Science College, Jammu" variant="bordered">
            <p>
              He also taught as a <strong>Lecturer at GGM Science College in Jammu</strong>, bringing his
              expertise to higher education. This position would place him in Jammu during one of the darkest
              moments of his life.
            </p>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="leaf" />

  <!-- 1947 Tragedy Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-kashmir-stone-grey/10">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-8 text-center">
          1947: Tragedy and Survival
        </h2>

        <KashidaBorder variant="floral" height="50px" class="mb-8 opacity-40" />

        <div class="kashmir-card p-8 border-l-8 border-kashmir-burgundy">
          <p class="text-lg text-kashmir-lake-blue/90 leading-relaxed mb-6">
            In <strong>1947</strong>, during the horrific violence of Partition, Abdul Aziz Bhat and his
            family were caught in the <strong>Jammu Massacre</strong>. He was <strong>31 years old</strong>,
            a young father and educator with his whole life ahead of him.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-white/50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-6">
            <h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-3">What Happened:</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-kashmir-lake-blue/90">
              <li>• The family was told they were being taken to safety on a bus</li>
              <li>• The bus went in a different direction than promised—into an ambush</li>
              <li>• He was shot while holding his infant daughter, <strong>Masooda</strong></li>
              <li>• The bullet passed through Masooda and blew off his <strong>left thumb</strong></li>
              <li>• Baby Masooda died from her wounds</li>
              <li>• His wife, <strong>Saideh</strong>, was injured with a head wound but survived</li>
              <li>• After the massacre, he eventually migrated to Srinagar</li>
              <li>• He lost his left thumb permanently—a reminder he carried for <strong>69 years</strong></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-kashmir-gold pl-6 italic text-kashmir-lake-blue/80 mb-6">
            "He carried the scar—both physical and emotional—for the rest of his life. But he refused
            to let tragedy define him. Instead, he let it fuel him."
          </blockquote>

          <div class="bg-kashmir-burgundy text-white p-6 rounded-lg">
            <h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-2xl mb-3">One Year Later...</h4>
            <p class="text-lg">
              In <strong>1948</strong>, just one year after this devastating loss, Abdul Aziz Bhat became
              a <strong>founding faculty member of the University of Kashmir</strong>.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-kashmir-gold font-semibold">
              From unspeakable tragedy to transformational legacy—in just twelve months.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="shikara" />

  <!-- University of Kashmir Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-8 text-center">
          Building the University "From the Rock" (1948)
        </h2>

        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <p class="text-xl text-kashmir-lake-blue/80 italic">
            "We built it from the rock—literally and figuratively."
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div class="kashmir-card p-8 bg-gradient-to-br from-kashmir-burgundy to-kashmir-crimson text-white">
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-6">The Founding (1948)</h3>
            <p class="text-lg mb-4">
              In <strong>1948</strong>, Abdul Aziz Bhat became one of the <strong>founding faculty members</strong>
              of the <strong>University of Kashmir</strong>. This wasn't just a ceremonial role—he was there at
              the very beginning, helping to create Kashmir's premier institution of higher learning.
            </p>
            <p class="text-lg">
              The phrase <em>"from the rock"</em> had two meanings:
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-white/90">
              <li><strong>Literally:</strong> He participated in the physical construction of the university buildings</li>
              <li><strong>Figuratively:</strong> He developed the curriculum for the Education department from scratch</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <Card title="His Roles at the University" variant="bordered">
            <ul class="space-y-4">
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-3 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <div>
                  <strong class="text-kashmir-burgundy">Professor of English</strong>
                  <p class="text-sm text-kashmir-lake-blue/70 mt-1">Teaching literature and language to generations of students</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-3 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <div>
                  <strong class="text-kashmir-burgundy">Social Worker</strong>
                  <p class="text-sm text-kashmir-lake-blue/70 mt-1">Pioneering social work education in Kashmir</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-3 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <div>
                  <strong class="text-kashmir-burgundy">Dean of Education</strong>
                  <p class="text-sm text-kashmir-lake-blue/70 mt-1">Leading the Education department and shaping pedagogy</p>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-start">
                <ChinaLeaf size="sm" color="outline" class="mr-3 mt-1 flex-shrink-0" />
                <div>
                  <strong class="text-kashmir-burgundy">Registrar</strong>
                  <p class="text-sm text-kashmir-lake-blue/70 mt-1">Administrative leadership of the entire university</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="leaf" />

  <!-- International Recognition Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-kashmir-cream">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-8 text-center">
          International Recognition
        </h2>

        <KashidaBorder variant="floral" height="60px" class="mb-12 opacity-40" />

        <div class="mughal-grid gap-8">
          <Card title="Oxford University, UK" variant="gradient">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
              <ShikaraIcon size="lg" variant="ornate" color="multi" />
            </div>
            <p class="text-white/90 mb-4">
              Abdul Aziz Bhat served as a <strong>Guest Lecturer at Oxford University</strong>, one of the
              world's most prestigious academic institutions.
            </p>
            <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">
              From a village in Kashmir to the halls of Oxford—an extraordinary journey of academic achievement.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <Card title="Warwick University, UK" variant="gradient">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
              <ShikaraIcon size="lg" variant="ornate" color="multi" />
            </div>
            <p class="text-white/90 mb-4">
              He also lectured at <strong>Warwick University</strong>, sharing his expertise in education and
              social work with British academics and students.
            </p>
            <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">
              His knowledge and perspective were valued on the international stage.
            </p>
          </Card>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="shikara" />

  <!-- Later Life & Legacy Section -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-kashmir-burgundy mb-8 text-center">
          A Century of Life (1916-2016)
        </h2>

        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <div class="flex justify-center space-x-4 mb-6">
            <ChinaLeaf size="lg" color="burgundy" animate={true} />
            <ChinaLeaf size="lg" color="gold" animate={true} />
            <ChinaLeaf size="lg" color="crimson" animate={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-kashmir-burgundy mb-2">100 Years</p>
          <p class="text-lg text-kashmir-lake-blue/70">
            Like the ancient chinar trees of Kashmir, he stood for a century
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <Card title="Family Man" variant="bordered" showLeafWatermark={true}>
            <p class="mb-4">
              Abdul Aziz and his wife Saideh raised <strong>six children</strong> together:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
              <li>1. <strong>Masooda</strong> (daughter) - Died as infant in 1947</li>
              <li>2. <strong>Yasmeen</strong> (daughter)</li>
              <li>3. <strong>Altaf</strong> (son) - Civil Engineer</li>
              <li>4. <strong>Javaid</strong> (son) - Pilot</li>
              <li>5. <strong>Shaheen</strong> (daughter)</li>
              <li>6. <strong>Afzal</strong> (son, born 1955) - Surgical Assistant</li>
            </ul>
          </Card>

          <Card title="Social Worker Throughout" variant="bordered">
            <p>
              Beyond his academic roles, Abdul Aziz Bhat dedicated himself to <strong>social work</strong>
              throughout his life. He believed education wasn't just about classrooms—it was about serving
              communities and lifting people up.
            </p>
          </Card>

          <div class="kashmir-card p-8 dal-lake-bg text-white">
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold mb-4">His Final Years</h3>
            <p class="text-lg mb-4">
              Abdul Aziz Bhat lived to be <strong>100 years old</strong>, passing away in <strong>2016</strong>.
              He witnessed a full century of Kashmir's history, from British colonial rule through independence,
              partition, and into the modern era.
            </p>
            <p class="text-white/90">
              He carried the scar of 1947—his missing left thumb—for <strong>69 years</strong>. But he also
              carried the pride of having built an institution that would educate <strong>thousands</strong>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SectionDivider icon="leaf" />

  <!-- Reflection Section -->
  <section class="section-padding-sm bg-gradient-to-b from-kashmir-cream to-white">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <blockquote class="p-12 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-2xl border-l-8 border-kashmir-burgundy">
          <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-kashmir-lake-blue italic leading-relaxed mb-6">
            "Sink your differences and Cement your relationships."
          </p>
          <cite class="text-lg text-kashmir-burgundy font-semibold not-italic">
            — Abdul Aziz Bhat
          </cite>
          <div class="flex justify-center space-x-3 mt-8">
            <ChinaLeaf size="md" color="burgundy" />
            <ChinaLeaf size="md" color="gold" />
            <ChinaLeaf size="md" color="burgundy" />
          </div>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="/legacy" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline">
            Explore His Legacy
          </a>
          <a href="/timeline" class="btn-secondary inline-block no-underline">
            View Full Timeline
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
